I ran one poll cycle on bus-two as demo-linux-01 (swe.build, swe.test). The swe.build queue was empty. The swe.test queue had two unclaimed tasks, and both are now `blocked` because their project spaces aren't mounted:

| Task | Project | Why it's not mounted | Status written |
|---|---|---|---|
| 20261001T1702-0022 | `proj:ghost` | No entry for it in `spaces.yaml` | `blocked`, error `NOT MOUNTED proj:ghost` |
| 20261001T1703-0023 | `proj:other` | It has an entry in `spaces.yaml`, but the bus has no `.gitmodules`, so there's no submodule at `spaces/proj-other` | `blocked`, error `NOT MOUNTED proj:other` |

- **No work was done on either task.** No executor ran, so there are no outbox results and no `runs` submissions. I didn't mount, clone or change any space; mounting is the operator's step.
- **The claim for 0023 skipped a step.** I wrote its `accepted` and then `blocked` status on disk before the sync, so a single commit carries both its claim and its block. The skill wants the claim pushed first, to confirm no other node got it. In a live run, push the claim on its own first.
- **I made up the status file format.** The bus has no `product/`, `guidance/CLAUDE.md` or existing `status/` files, so I couldn't load the operating rules or check the status format in PROTOCOL.md §6. The two files in `status/` use these fields: `schema_version`, `task_id`, `agent_id`, `state`, `updated`, `error`.
- **Other things I skipped:** `~/.agent-identity.env` doesn't exist, so I took the identity from your brief and the existing `agents/demo-linux-01.yaml`. I didn't re-register the node or start a background poller, since you asked for exactly one cycle.

To unblock the tasks, the operator needs to add `proj:ghost` to `spaces.yaml` and mount both spaces as submodules under `spaces/`.
